[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I built the feature table **`recsa355e6`, version 1** on the Hopsworks platform with all work running platform-side via the `hops` CLI.
[agent] **Approach (everything on-platform):**
[agent] 1. **Ingested** the three input files as offline feature groups (`user_emb`, `item_emb`, `interactions`) via `hops fg create` + `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. **Computed** the recommendations entirely in Trino (`hops sql`, platform-side compute): cross-joined users×items, took the dot product of the 8-dim embeddings as relevance, excluded already-interacted pairs with `NOT EXISTS`, ranked with `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY user_id ORDER BY score DESC, item_id ASC)`, and kept rank ≤ 5.
[agent] 3. **Wrote** the 200 result rows into `recsa355e6` v1, created `--online` (online_enabled=true), so features are available for both offline reads and low-latency online lookup.
[agent] **Verification:**
[agent] - 200 rows = 40 users × 5 ranks; every user has exactly ranks 1–5.
[agent] - `rec_id` formatted `<user_id>#<rank>` (e.g. `U0000#1`); columns exactly `rec_id, user_id, rank, item_id`.
[agent] - Exclusion check via Trino: **0 violations** — no recommended item was previously interacted with.
[agent] - `online_enabled: true` confirmed; both offline (`fg preview`) and online stores populated by the insert.
[agent] **One adaptation worth noting:** the FG schema's `rank:int` was rejected on insert because the JSON loader infers integers as `bigint`; I recreated the column as `bigint` (still an integer type, values 1–5) to match. Also, the cluster serves an IP-SAN-mismatched TLS cert, so all calls used `--no-verify`.
